# Gate step 1561-47a8 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. The end-user installers print only end-user lines (1561-9f4x;
# operator ruling 2026-10-08: "we do not need to print any power user messages
# during install, at all ... a pretty installer, rather than an
# informational/debugging installer"). Diagnostic detail goes to the install log
# and is shown by path only on failure.
#
# The step runs scripts/lua/check-installer-end-user-output.lua over the real
# tree (enforcing the per-installer floors: install-windows.ps1 0;
# install.sh and install-macos.sh at today's counts until their slices
# 1561-y6f9 / 1561-kfgk drop them). Its fixture (scratch copies: a flag-naming
# line refused by file:line, the `# power-user-only` and PENDING-1560-UAM3
# exemptions, a comment not counted, install.sh above its floor refused) is
# scripts/lua/test-check-installer-end-user-output.lua, run inline by build.sh
# because it needs the runner binary a STEP_LUA does not receive. Both are Lua:
# the first draft's .sh pair would have added two items to the shell ratchet.
# Pre-fix: FAILS, install-windows.ps1 printed 21. Pure source reads.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the end-user installers print only end-user lines (1561-47a8)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/check-installer-end-user-output.lua"
STEP_ERROR="an end-user installer prints power-user or diagnostic text again (1561-9f4x); see the file:line above"
STEP_OK="the end-user installers print only end-user lines (at or below their floors)"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="yolanda-windows 2026-10-10 msys ok:installer-end-user-output"
